{"title":"2016 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Stephanie has 1000 eggs to pack into cartons of 12 eggs. While packing the eggs, she breaks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> eggs. The unbroken eggs completely fill a collection of cartons with no eggs left over. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f02c98d38a62c294b00b4d182dda7b8ca083f61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Finding each fraction as a decimal, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b551b5747bc67f4ea6267afb4d936461f972c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3} = 0.\\overline{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f73e65672b3478c3a8005f6842ef8b9ae642422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4} = 0.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33f0c00fde4729424a905f6229c2bd038b1d34e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{6} = 0.8\\overline{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8e5d6b31951955ead24a2317a0a2e72db62378a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{8} = 0.625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/6/2b6608a9bd5554346a71646a6d30b899417d23da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{12} = 0.91\\overline{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Of these, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3ba538b404820c88f630374f5d30d419bd9158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f493f2809dd8cacc1016bd957689fe8bdc0b631e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{5}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"24\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the LCM of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> from either factors, prime factorization, etc, so we can use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as a common denominator:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1eb8e64006d43efcdf560cc309ac273ab4aec6fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2 \\times 8}{3 \\times 8} = \\frac{16}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"93\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1de2767bd9394819dd0987875c8d41c12c2897fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3 \\times 6}{4 \\times 6} = \\frac{18}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"93\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a48f685bd61e0b5b7a37cefa49ad3780038e70e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5 \\times 4}{6 \\times 4} = \\frac{20}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"93\" height=\"40\" /> (we can also realize that this is automatically more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f4344e4ce1c2a266b885d9b160544e3036de15f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> since it as the same numerator but a lower denominator, so we can technically skip it)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e07a664d1282994e633d680f2e3d27e895d238b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5 \\times 3}{8 \\times 3} = \\frac{15}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"93\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/7110d75cd73935efa5d22404adf7e4edde985315.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11 \\times 2}{12 \\times 2} = \\frac{22}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"102\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Of these fractions, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/533234a3bab4f87c01175beae10e5f8bf154e48a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> is the smallest since it has the lowest numerator and all of the fractions have the same denominator, meaning that the smallest of the original list is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f493f2809dd8cacc1016bd957689fe8bdc0b631e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{5}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"24\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19a8bd8aca3f3014f785e348c3e74f0d8df17858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3} = 1 - \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6d4dfdfb5c8c4e43247294f8a179d26872592c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4} = 1 - \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/491d19a9c478cbadb1f840895dca286baed5b650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{6} = 1 - \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff74f94828b31109f682dad472d854795e0f2f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{12} = 1 - \\frac{1}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is the largest of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d8e9c9a8850b0b6eb3ee534bd1d4b15b575db11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{1}{6},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e10f7b229549d9afbdef6ae2862bc89bacfe16cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> since the numerators are the same but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest denominator, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> must be the smallest fraction in that list. This reduces the number of fractions we actually have to compare to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f4344e4ce1c2a266b885d9b160544e3036de15f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Next, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b551b5747bc67f4ea6267afb4d936461f972c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3} = 0.\\overline{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8e5d6b31951955ead24a2317a0a2e72db62378a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{8} = 0.625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />. Of these, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3ba538b404820c88f630374f5d30d419bd9158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.625$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f493f2809dd8cacc1016bd957689fe8bdc0b631e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{5}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"24\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC\" title=\"2016 CIMC\">2016 CIMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CIMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CIMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2016 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2016 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2016 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2016 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CIMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2016 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Intermediate_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Intermediate Competition\">CEMC Intermediate Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018061132\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.110 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 230/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1246/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 143/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7555/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.808      1 Template:CEMC_CIMC/CSMC_box\n100.00%    6.808      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37147:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018061132 and revision id 286996. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}